('CIT_MYC_DIWIA_VENTRI','ENT_MYC_DIWIA','SRC_VENTRIS_CHADWICK','Ventris & Chadwick, Documents in Mycenaean Greek','Ventris & Chadwick, Documents in Mycenaean Greek','di-wi-ja in PY 28 = An42 is probably a variant spelling (DiwjafDiwia, cf. me-u-jofme-wi-jo) of the genitive (Diwias doe/a) ; also without context on KN X 97. Cf. the goddess b.lflO: in a Pamphylian inscription (Schwyzer, Dial. 686, I), said to be the Magna Mater.','Ventris & Chadwick',1973,'None',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'Linear B attestation — brief flagged excerpt; verify the tablet.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_MYC_DRIMIOS_VENTRI','ENT_MYC_DRIMIOS','SRC_VENTRIS_CHADWICK','Ventris & Chadwick, Documents in Mycenaean Greek','Tn 316,','To Drimios the priest of Zeus : one gold bowl, [one man?]. (4th) blank. (5th) P Y L O S : blank. RE V E R S E : (In the month?) of ? Plowi(s)tos: (1st) P Y L O S : perform a certain action at the place Pa-ki-ja-ne, and bring the gifts and bring those to carry them. To the Mistress : one gold cup, one woman. (2nd) To ? Mnasa : one gold bowl, one woman. To Posidaeia: one gold bowl, one woman. (3rd) To the '' thrice-hero '' : one gold cup.','Ventris & Chadwick',1973,'None',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'Linear B attestation — brief flagged excerpt; verify the tablet.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_MYC_ENYALIOS_VENTRI','ENT_MYC_ENYALIOS','SRC_VENTRIS_CHADWICK','Ventris & Chadwick, Documents in Mycenaean Greek','Tn 316:','the epithet "Ap11a (ace.) applied to Zeus and Enyalios, and "Ape1av, "Ap11av to Athena, in a fourth-century inscription from Arcadian Orchomenos, Schwyzer, Dial. 665c. The connexion with "Ap11s is doubtful, unless the Aeol. "Apevs, ''Ape\iios is secondary. diwjo- ''of Zeus '' : note the different spelling (and meaning?) of di-wi-ja on 28 -An42.','Ventris & Chadwick',1973,'None',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'Linear B attestation — brief flagged excerpt; verify the tablet.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_MYC_IPHIMEDEIA_VENTRI','ENT_MYC_IPHIMEDEIA','SRC_VENTRIS_CHADWICK','Ventris & Chadwick, Documents in Mycenaean Greek','Tn 316','At Pylos we find Iphimedeia, a semi-mythical figure in Homer, apparently receiving divine honours. The identity of the other deities is unknown or conjectural. The offerings recorded at Knossos differ from those at Pylos in that livestock are rarely mentioned. None of the tablets dealing with livestock can be proved to have any religious significance, though this is not always impossible; t Sundwall''s theory ofhecatombs must be abandoned (see p. 198).','Ventris & Chadwick',1973,'None',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'Linear B attestation — brief flagged excerpt; verify the tablet.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_MYC_PANTHEON_VENTRI','ENT_MYC_PANTHEON','SRC_VENTRIS_CHADWICK','Ventris & Chadwick, Documents in Mycenaean Greek','Ventris & Chadwick, Documents in Mycenaean Greek','DOCUMENTS IN MYCENAEAN GREEK S E C O ND EDIT I O N PLATE I 46=Aul02, Mycenaean tablet of''page'' shape DOCUMENTS IN MYCENAEAN GREEK FIRST E DITION BY MICHAEL VENTRIS AND JOHN CHADWICK W!Til A FOREWORD BY THE LATE ALAN J. B.','Ventris & Chadwick',1973,'None',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'Linear B attestation — brief flagged excerpt; verify the tablet.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_MYC_POTNIA_VENTRI','ENT_MYC_POTNIA','SRC_VENTRIS_CHADWICK','Ventris & Chadwick, Documents in Mycenaean Greek','An 1281','But in other tablets from both Knossos and Pylos Potnia appears as a divine name standing by itself(e .g. KN 205 = Gg702, M 729, PY FnO l , 172 = Kn02, Vn07) . 1 26 THE E V I D E N C E O F T HE TABLETS No evidence which would identify this deity has so far appeared, and thus none of the guesses can be tested ; she seems to be of some importance, but is not necessarily the protectress of Pylos.','Ventris & Chadwick',1973,'None',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'Linear B attestation — brief flagged excerpt; verify the tablet.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
('CIT_MYC_POTNIA_LABYRINTH_VENTRI','ENT_MYC_POTNIA_LABYRINTH','SRC_VENTRIS_CHADWICK','Ventris & Chadwick, Documents in Mycenaean Greek','Gg 702','M P H O R A 1 One jar of honey to all the gods, One jar of honey to the Mistress of the ?Labyrinth. da-pu2?-ri-to-Jo (gen.): this place-name probably recurs in the da-pu-ri-to-[ of the frag­ mcnta.ry X 140, and might conceivably be a fuller spelling of the Da-*22-to of Knossos and Elcusis. To identify it with t.a!)vp1V6os involves the highly uncertain assumption that the initial consonant has some intermediate sound peculiar to ''Aegean ''. But cf.','Ventris & Chadwick',1973,'None',NULL,'primary-verbatim',NULL,true,'Linear B attestation — brief flagged excerpt; verify the tablet.',DATE '2026-06-18','name-anchored (note-keyword scored) + substring gate; locus per attestation',1),
